  "notes": "Sketches, DXF profiles, a centered NEMA17 clearance mounting plate, STEP parts and a native model. Plate: 60 x 60 x 4mm; 31mm bolt pitch, four 3.6mm M3 clearance holes; centered 8mm shaft bore and 22.4mm x 2.2mm top boss relief. Dimensions checked against STEPPERONLINE 17HS19-2004S1 drawing A0842; the clearance allowances are demo design choices, not a tested physical fit or load rating. The Plate started from Sample Parts/plate.camproject and is saved here with its edge bevels modeled into the part. The X part keeps its original STEP geometry; it is roughed with a 6mm long-flute end mill and drilled with a 5mm drill. Generate all or explore each setup in Simulate.\nPlate material: 6061-T6 aluminum (assumed). These cutters, speeds and setups are demo values that have not been proven on a real machine, so check them against your own machine and tooling before you cut. The outer edge gets two descending passes for a 0.5mm x45deg bevel; the four bolt hole mouths, the boss mouth and the recessed shaft mouth each get one 0.25mm x45deg edge-break pass. Bottom edges are not beveled: reaching them needs the part flipped in a second setup. The working diameters stay sharp below the bevels, the boss floor stays at Z1.8 and the part bottom at Z0. Bevel cutter: pointed 6mm 90deg 2-flute; tip offsets outer 1.3, bolts 1.35, boss and shaft 1.4mm; 31000 RPM; feeds outer 900, bolts 250, boss 800, shaft 600, plunge 100 mm/min.",
